aim challenged and the distinction asserted. Clarify mode semantics; do not transfer the reader labels mechanically. Context22b:7 producer propositions explicitly say Rav Nachman rules and retain both clauses despite generic position local-status strings. This is reduced specificity, not denial of the local ruling.\n\n## Reader-side findings and supported uncertainty\n\n**R1 — context22b:11 typed question omitted by the reader.** `nd118.claims.026` narrates repeated yes answers; the reader questions-layer coverage is none-found. Original `אמרי ליה נדרת אדעתא דהכי אמר אין אדעתא דהכי אין כמה זימנין` contains explicit questions. Producer `nd.r023.againq.q` and `nd.r023.yes.answer` preserve them. This is a context reader omission and cannot be charged to production or to the 30-core sample.\n\nReader edge020 at23a:7 labels the direct `אמר לו לא והתירו רבי יוסי` answer editorial reconstruction. The answer relation is directly stated; treating its existence as source-explicit is better. Reader edge021's cross-story support relation can remain editorial interpretation; producer's analogy relation is reasonable.\n\nAt25a:4 reader claim063 resolves `אמר ליה ללווה זיל פרע לי` as the creditor's demand. The first-person `לי` supports that interpretation, but the immediate clause does not explicitly name its speaker; producer `nd.r025.pay.c` conservatively retains the demand with uncertainty. Keep this as a supported interpretive difference, not a producer error. At23a:4 both preserve the difficult `ושריה לנפשיה` without deriving general permission to annul one's own vow.\n\n## Reasonable granularity and retained positive evidence\n\nThe reader creates per-segment structure records and seven explicit continuation edges; production groups relevant segments into larger structures. Both exact partitions validate. Whole structures may include unreviewed material: this comparison certifies only the 45 named references, not their other segments or all closed-boundary decisions. The re